      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. So if I were to add a base like baking soda to a recipe to speed up the browning, I'm essentially just manipulating that nucleophilicity? Also, can you elaborate more on the Amadori rearrangement? I want to make sure I explain the transition from the Schiff base to the ketosamine correctly in my literature review.",
      "source": "evaluator"
